    "beneficial_predator_notes": [
      "Natural enemies can assist significantly in the control of imported cabbageworm. Important parasitoids include the pupal, larval, and egg parasitoids in the Trichogramma genus, as well as tachinid flies. Timely mass releases of commercially available trichogramma during peak flight can be an effective control agent. Viruses and bacterial diseases are also sometimes important control factors in the field. If possible, use Bacillus thuringiensis to avoid adverse impact on natural enemies. Bacillus thuringiensis is very effective against imported cabbageworm, especially when applied to young (early-instar) caterpillars."
